    "checks": [
      "Local lifetime caps at minimum, default and maximum configured refresh intervals exclude two seconds of simulated lookup time.",
      "A shorter upstream TTL and an equal TTL/cap remain bounded; zero TTL or expiry at/before return is rejected.",
      "One nanosecond of remaining lifetime is usable with emitted TTL zero; expiry at the exact bound and afterwards returns SERVFAIL.",
      "Success immediately before the deadline remains accepted; completion at/after it, observed context expiry, explicit parent cancellation and an earlier parent deadline are rejected.",
      "Partial addresses accompanying a resolver error are not accepted.",
      "A/AAAA replies in both TCP/UDP Answer modes remain cache-only; rejection removes old addresses, accounting stays correct, and a subsequent valid refresh recovers."
    ],
    "counting": "Count 17 table cases once. Four family/transport calls, repeated boundary assertions, before/after runs and the race rerun are not added as separate cases."
