  "limitations": [
    "The new resolver-return tests establish cache admission behavior, not a remotely exploitable pinned-resolver cancellation race.",
    "The trusted Resolver implementation must eventually return and honor context cancellation; this change does not forcibly stop arbitrary resolver code that never returns.",
    "Rejection is based on each lookup completion. This does not claim batch-wide cancellation fencing or a deployment boundary.",
    "No new Snort SID or universal RFC, W3C, zero-day or hostile-agent prevention claim follows from these checks."
